X believed that music contains both healing and destructive frequencies that are intentionally manipulated.

He has been very vocal in interviews, on socials, and songs about his relationship with spirituality.

He believed that most music out there is engineered down to the frequency level to manipulate certain emotions.

Hertz, kilohertz, megahertz, and ultra-hertz— he mentioned that channeling these frequencies can be used to trigger certain parts of the mind in listeners.

He says most artists don’t care enough to go that deep into the art of music, so producers and executives manipulate these sounds on their behalf.

X called it “brainwashing,” and said that just listening to an artist’s music and perceived image doesn’t mean you know the artist as a person.

Ye expressed very similar ideas when discussing how the 808 beat in today’s rap music unconsciously lowers your frequency. He also mentioned how music today is designed to influence mood, behavior, at scale.
